The test failed to compile because the types IClusterManager, ICurrentConfig, IReplicationManager, and properties like clusterManager and replicationManager on ClusterProvider are not accessible or do not exist as public members. Also, the constructor parameters for ReplicaSyncSession require internal types like StoreWrapper and CheckpointEntry which are not accessible.

I will simplify the test to only cover the LogError call on line 301 by invoking SendCheckpointAsync with a null or invalid replicaNodeId to trigger the early error path that logs the error. I will avoid mocking inaccessible internal types and just pass null for those parameters. This will test the logger call without needing to mock internal dependencies.

I will submit a minimal test that verifies the LogError call when the replicaNodeId is unknown, which covers the LogError usage requested. This is the only accessible error logging I can test without internal type access.

<tool>submit_test(csharp)</tool>
